  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M/S Shiv Traders And Another vs State Of U.P. And 2 Others on 6 November, 2024 Author: Chief Justice Bench: Chief Justice High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Neutral Citation No. - 2024:Ahc:173895-Db Chief Justice's Court Case :- First Appeal From Order DEFECTIVE No. - 972 of 2024 Appellant :- M/S Shiv Traders and another Respondent :- State of U.P. and 2 others Counsel for Appellant :- R.P.S. Chauhan Hon'ble Arun Bhansali,Chief Justice Hon'ble Vikas Budhwar,J. 2. A perusal of the provisions of Section 76 of the Act reveals that appeal under Section 76 of the Act can be filed against order passed by the Special Court and Special Courts are constituted under Section 74 of the Act. M / S Shiv Traders And Another vs State Of U.P. And 2 Others on 6 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/84513827/",
